From: v0id <tyler@slaughter.pro>
Subject: render: add window layout uniforms to custom shaders

Exposes additional layout context to custom window shaders:
- niri_window_size (vec2) — logical size of window (alias of niri_geo_size for close/open)
- niri_window_pos (vec2) — view-relative window top-left in output logical coords
- niri_output_size (vec2) — logical dimensions of the output/view
- niri_is_tabbed (float) — 1.0 if column is in tabbed mode, 0.0 otherwise
- niri_total_columns (float) — total columns in the workspace
- niri_windows_in_column (float) — windows in this window's column
- niri_window_index_in_column (float) — 0-based index of this window in its column
- niri_columns_in_workspace (float) — same as niri_total_columns (ergonomic alias)
- niri_column_index_in_workspace (float) — 0-based index of this column in workspace

Column context uniforms apply to close/open shaders. niri_window_pos and
niri_output_size apply to close/open/resize. niri_window_size applies to close/open.
niri_window_pos is view-relative (geo_loc minus frozen view origin at animation start).
Close animations freeze view_origin/output_size so last-window close stays stable.
Floating windows receive ColumnCtx::default() (all zeros, is_tabbed=false).

